+    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+    // os8088: the mechanical timing model.
+    //
+    // Stock MartyPC hands a sector over the instant it is asked for. There is
+    // no platter, no rotational latency and no interleave, which is why it
+    // reads a 16 KB file ~30x faster than the IBM 5150 this project is
+    // calibrated against (PERFORMANCE.md Part 9 Set 11). Everything below
+    // exists so that the three raw `int 13h` rows Sets 14/22 measured on that
+    // machine come out right, and they come out of ONE mechanism:
+    //
+    //   one sector, repeated  199 ms  = 1.00 revolution
+    //   a 9-sector track, 1 call      384 ms = 1.92 revolutions
+    //   the same 9 sectors, 9 calls   2,005 ms = 10.02 revolutions
+    //
+    // A sector is readable only as it passes the head, so all three are the
+    // same statement about where the platter is when the command arrives.
+    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
